Aye, the Cailleach o' the Hill — sure, every soul in these parts knows her name. 'Tis said she spins wool by moonlight and leaves offerings at the sídhe for the folk that dwell below. Some call her a witch, others say she's a spirit bound to the old ways. I mind me own grandmother spoke of her not with fear, but with respect — we'd best do the same, or 'twill bring bad luck to the parish.

